    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60">

                <pb facs="0045" n="41" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg41"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.116/142: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-23T18:00:00-04:00">August 23, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>295. Peiping’s 505, August 18, 4 p.m., and Tientsin’s 157, August 18, 1 p.m., in
                    regard to embargo on wireless equipment at Tientsin. Department desires that you
                    make appropriate representations to the Japanese Foreign Office in regard to
                    this matter. Following the general lines of your recent approach in the matter
                    of the embargo on hides and skins, you may point out that the embargo on
                    importation of wireless equipment is an unwarranted restriction on American
                    trade interests which are the principal suppliers of such equipment; and that
                    the holding up of equipment ordered before the embargo was imposed is causing
                    American dealers substantial losses.</p>
                <p>Department desires that you request that steps be taken to have the embargo
                    removed and that special action be taken promptly to relieve the importers in
                    respect to equipment ordered prior to the embargo.<anchor n="63" xml:id="d60-f1"
                    /></p>
                <p>Peiping please repeat to Chungking and Tientsin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d60-f1" n="63" xml:id="d60-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 558, August 26, 4 p.m., the Ambassador in Japan informed the
                    Department that oral representations, supported by an <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi>, were presented to the Japanese Foreign Office that same
                    day (693.116144).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
